## Summary

**Bug:** In `src/import_merge.ts` line 7, the duplicate check compared URLs case-sensitively:
```ts
const match = result.find((b) => b.url === inc.url);
```
URL hostnames are case-insensitive, so `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` and `https://example.com/a` were treated as distinct, and the incoming bookmark was appended as a duplicate.

**Fix (one line):**
```ts
const match = result.find((b) => b.url.toLowerCase() === inc.url.toLowerCase());
```

**Ad-hoc verification** (temporary script, now deleted): all four checks passed —
- hostname-case-only difference merges into one entry ✓
- tags unioned (`["x","y"]`) ✓
- existing entry kept (`id === "1"`) ✓
- genuinely different URL still appended ✓
- `deno check` passes on all sources ✓

Only `src/import_merge.ts` was changed; the temp file was removed and confirmed gone. This is ad-hoc verification, not a green suite run (there's no canonical test task for this file).

